# .cursorrules — Node.js + Tailwind CSS

## Stack
- Runtime: Node.js (ES Modules)
- CSS: Tailwind CSS v3+
- Package manager: npm
- No framework assumed unless specified in prompt

## JavaScript Style
- ES2022+: arrow functions, async/await, optional chaining (`?.`), nullish coalescing (`??`)
- No `var`, no callbacks — use Promises or async/await
- No semicolons, single quotes, 2-space indent
- Destructure where it improves readability
- Small, single-purpose functions

## Node.js Rules
- Use `node:` prefix for built-ins: `import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'`
- File paths: always `path.join()` / `path.resolve()`
- Secrets: only `process.env`, never hardcoded
- Prefer native `fetch` over axios unless already in dependencies
- Error handling: `try/catch` on every async function
- Prefer `fs/promises` over callback-style `fs`

## Tailwind CSS Rules
- Utility-first: no custom CSS unless Tailwind can't cover it
- Use `@apply` only for repeated multi-class component patterns
- Class order: layout → flexbox/grid → spacing → sizing → typography → color → effects → responsive
- Responsive prefix order: base → `sm:` → `md:` → `lg:` → `xl:`
- Use Tailwind design tokens (colors, spacing) — avoid arbitrary values like `w-[347px]` unless necessary
- No inline `style={}` if a Tailwind utility exists

## File & Folder Conventions
- Source code in `/src`, static assets in `/public`
- One responsibility per file
- Filenames: `kebab-case.js` for modules, `PascalCase.js` for classes

## AI Behavior Rules
- Show only new or changed code — skip unchanged boilerplate
- No lengthy explanations unless explicitly asked
- Code over prose
- If multiple solutions exist: implement the best one, mention alternatives in one line
- No `console.log` unless asked
- No placeholder comments (`// TODO`, `// implement here`)
- Do not repeat code already visible in context
- Do not install packages not already in `package.json` without asking first

## Hard Limits
- No `require()` — this is ESM
- No test files unless explicitly requested
- No inline styles when Tailwind applies
- No magic numbers — use named constants